cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ReviewConverge, please cite it as below."
title: "ReviewConverge: A Convergence Benchmark and Workflow Standard for Iterative Agentic Review"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark and metric standard that treats the per-round finding-set of an
  iterative LLM review loop as the unit of convergence, classifies each run as
  contractive-to-correct / oscillatory-churn / false-convergence / divergent
  against seeded ground truth, and compares workflow interventions that make the
  loop converge to a correct fixed point.
type: software
version: 0.0.1
date-released: 2026-01-01
license: MIT
keywords:
  - large language models
  - agentic review
  - convergence
  - benchmark
  - evaluation
authors:
  - family-names: "Phanvilai"
    given-names: "Sittiphol"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-6956-0233"
